    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0499" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg451"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dix</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No<hi rendition="#italic">.</hi> 195.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 20, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>S<hi rendition="#small-caps">ir</hi>: I have your dispatch of the 7th of August,
                    No. 254. Certainly no one could object to the delay which Mr. Moustier finds it
                    necessary to make in regard to entering into negotiations upon the
                    naturalization question.</p>
                <p>I hope, however, that you will improve the earliest moment of convenience on the
                    part of the French government for bringing the subject to a conclusion, so that
                    the treaty, if one shall be made, can be submitted to the United States Senate
                    as soon as it shall have reassembled.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John</hi> A. D<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >ix</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>.,<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
